# iOS Outgoing plugin registration HARD LOCK

**HARD LOCK (2026-07-28, registration model 2026-10-01).** Full doc: `docs/dibay-call-ios-outgoing-package-classlist-hard-lock.md`.

## Why

The Capacitor CLI regenerates `ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json` `packageClassList` from node_modules on every `cap copy` / `cap update` / `cap sync`. App-target plugins listed there were lost (`95e8100bc`, again 2026-10-01) → `Error loading plugin NativeCallService` breaks **iOS outgoing** while **incoming** CallKit/VoIP can still work.

Since 2026-10-01 App-target plugins are registered natively: `DibayRootBridgeViewController.makeAppTargetPlugins()` → `bridge.registerPluginInstance` in `capacitorDidLoad()`.

## Required (Call outgoing only)

- `NativeCallServicePlugin`
- `DibayVoipCallPlugin`
- `DibayCallPipPlugin`

Single list (full App-target list including Auth/Delivery/Device): `scripts/ios-app-target-plugins.mjs`.
Call subset export: `IOS_CALL_OUTGOING_PLUGIN_CLASSES`.

Auth launcher registration is **not** owned by this rule — see `docs/auth-ios-native-oauth-launcher-contract.md`.

## DO NOT (without explicit user approval)

- Remove the Call plugins above from `makeAppTargetPlugins()`
- Add them back into `packageClassList` (double load) or rewrite that file after the CLI
- “Fix” outgoing by web/Vercel-only redeploy when the plugin is missing from the installed App.app
- Embed `NativeOAuthLauncherPlugin` / Auth registration into this Call HARD LOCK

## Verify

```bash
npm run verify:ios-call-package-classlist-contract
node scripts/ios-app-target-plugins.mjs
```
